      "skill_tags": ["algebraic_fractions", "simplifying_expressions"],
      "problem_text": "Simplify $\\frac{x^2 + 4x + 3}{x + 1} + \\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3}$",
      "answer": "$2x + 6$",
      "solution": "$\\frac{x^2+4x+3}{x+1} = \\frac{(x+1)(x+3)}{x+1} = x+3$ (for $x \\neq -1$). $\\frac{x^2-9}{x-3} = \\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3} = x+3$ (for $x \\neq 3$). Sum: $(x+3)+(x+3)=2x+6$"
