      "answer": "$(2x+5)(3x-2)$ or $(3x-2)(2x+5)$ or $(6x-5)(x+2)$ etc.",
      "solution": "We need $ac=6$, $ad+bc=11$, $bd=-10$. Factor pairs for 6: (1,6),(2,3),(3,2),(6,1),(-1,-6),(-2,-3),(-3,-2),(-6,-1). Factor pairs for -10: (1,-10),(-1,10),(2,-5),(-2,5),(5,-2),(-5,2),(10,-1),(-10,1). Trying $(2x+5)(3x-2)$: FOIL gives $6x^2 -4x + 15x -10 = 6x^2 + 11x -10$. Works! So $a=2,b=5,c=3,d=-2$ (and swapped $a=3,b=-2,c=2,d=5$)."
